cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use these certificates or verifiers, please cite this release."
title: "MathIS Sidon Frontier: Exact R9 and R16 Certificates"
authors:
  - family-names: "Williams"
    given-names: "Ariel M."
version: "1.1.0"
date-released: "2026-10-17"
type: software
repository-code: "https://github.com/FromAriel/mathis-sidon-frontier"
abstract: >-
  Exact rational R9 and R16 certificates developed within the Hou-Zhao
  finite Sidon smoothing framework, with standalone standard-library Python
  verifiers, expected outputs and development history. Historical coefficient
  improvements superseded by stronger external results; no exponent
  improvement, optimality or solution of Erdos Problem 30 is claimed.
keywords:
  - Sidon sets
  - additive combinatorics
  - exact rational certificate
  - computer-assisted proof
  - Mathematical Integrity System
license: MIT
